  "interpretation": "Across #381, the first DATA packets for all three ACKNACK-requested sequences were visible on loopback but no matching EGO recvfrom row appeared before ACKNACK. Exact-reader retransmissions followed 5.117-5.193 ms after ACKNACK and then appeared at recvfrom. Near initial sequence 397, adjacent receive counters rose 781 to 793 and sampled socket drops rose from 781 to 791 2.333 ms after the first capture. This places the first-send absence before EGO recvfrom and makes socket queue overflow a plausible explanation, but the cumulative socket-wide counter cannot identify the specific dropped packet. A sequence-set intersection alone can be masked by a retransmission later inside the same interval.",
  "limitations": [
    "The SO_RXQ_OVFL value is cumulative for the UDP socket and covers traffic beyond the captured mapping-writer DATA rows; it cannot name an skb that was dropped before user-space receive.",
    "The run is one planner-only repeat; it is not a long-duration loss-rate characterization or a P2/GOAL C stage exit.",
    "Kernel eBPF/perf tracing remains unavailable in this environment because CAP_BPF and CAP_PERFMON are absent.",
    "No QoS, socket buffer, freshness threshold, control behavior, or canonical source/config was changed.",
    "A sequence-set overlap does not distinguish first delivery from a retransmission received within the interval; use the per-request first-capture/ACKNACK/recvfrom timeline."
  ],
